            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0267" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60F8/8</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Czechoslovak Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurban</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-09">July 9, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have been instructed to inform
                    Your Excellency that the Czechoslovak Government will discontinue, as far as the
                    United States is concerned, the use of import certificates in connection with
                    the export of Czechoslovak rye, barley, oats, and malt to the United States.</p>
                <p>The use of import certificates is specified in the Czechoslovak Law of June 5,
                    1930, Number 73 of the Collection of Laws and Decrees.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>V. I. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurban</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
